# Every PR adds its line under the next version's headings, so each merge of main into an open PR
# would conflict here. The union driver keeps the lines of both sides, this branch's first, and a
# line both sides rewrote stays twice: after a merge of main the author checks for that and keeps
# one (docs/TESTING.md → Reviewing a PR's tests).
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
# Claude Code reads the architecture's front matter (`paths`), and architecture.test.ts with it: kept
# with LF line endings on every checkout, Windows' core.autocrlf included.
.claude/rules/** text eol=lf
